{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And the she-ass saw, etc.</b> One needs to know HaShem's intention in this matter — that the angel was revealed to the she-ass, and also the stationing of the angel three times in three places, and the crushing of Balaam's leg, and her lying down, and also the opening of the she-ass's mouth — and the entire affair recounted here is a sealed matter." "It appears that the entire intention of HaShem in this matter was nothing but to humble the pride of this contemptible one, because he had earlier conducted himself with haughtiness before HaShem, as we wrote above — for he did not tell the princes that he goes by HaShem's permission, but rather as a man who stands in his own authority. Therefore HaShem sought for him a degradation lower than which there is none, and mocked him with a freakish and extraordinary disgrace. And it is a known thing that the vital animation which HaShem implanted in non-speaking animals is different from the vital animation that HaShem acted and made in speaking animals. Therefore, when HaShem wished the she-ass to open her mouth to speak like speaking animals, it was necessary to implant in her the vital animation of speaking animals — and this is what HaShem effected through the act of stationing the angel in three places and the she-ass's seeing the angel three times. For the power of speech requires three preparatory stages to precede it: they are the power of growth, which exists in all created beings; and the power of motion; and afterward the power of speech. Therefore he stood the first time and the she-ass saw him, and through the power of spiritual vision there was activated in her one mode of implanting the power of growth, by which the power of speech would be received; and he stood a second time and she saw him, and there was activated in her the power of motion, in which the power of speech is received; and the third time the power of speech was activated in her, and then HaShem opened her mouth and she spoke words of understanding in the manner of question and answer, and she shamed Balaam in a degrading manner before his servants, etc. And a disgrace that comes about in this manner carries a voice, because it is a wondrous thing in two respects: one respect, that a beast should speak; and the second, that a great man such as Balaam had his she-ass as a mate lying in his bosom." "<b>It remains</b> to know why the angel stood in three different places — he could have appeared to her three times in one place. Perhaps it is because he did to him corresponding to three things he did in his wickedness. First: HaShem said to him once <b>you shall not go, you shall not curse</b>, yet he did not say to the princes the statement 'you shall not curse,' etc. — and this was a cause to send others; and corresponding to this, he stood once in the road and the she-ass turned aside from the road, just as he turned aside from the path that HaShem had told him, as mentioned. Second: HaShem said to him, if <b>to call you</b> etc. — which makes the matter conditional, until he would know for certain that HaShem has satisfaction in the matter; and in this He hinted to him that he has no satisfaction and he did not feel it. And corresponding to this, the angel stood in a narrow path between the vineyards, and the she-ass crushed his leg — to say that HaShem pressured him, with the pleasantness of His words, to gain understanding, to do good, so that he would not go. Third: HaShem said to him at the time of the travel's permission, <b>but only the matter</b> etc. — and this statement is precisely measured; there is no room to deviate with its meaning this way or that; yet the wicked one proceeded with a different plan, as we inferred from the statement 'he was going' and also his statement 'and he was riding' etc., 'and his two servants' etc. And this corresponds to what the angel stood in a narrow place where there was no path, etc., and the she-ass lay down beneath him — which hints to say that HaShem does not desire the path upon which he desires to walk."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:12:52.009948465Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}